# Companion-module deploy-time parameters. Append the blocks you need to the REPO-ROOT `.env` (the one
# file every app and script reads; the module apps resolve the outermost workspaces root, so a
# `source/modules/.env` is never loaded). The core keys (WAF_WEB_ACL_ARN, ...) are in the
# repo-root `.env.example`.

# --- Streaming-media WAF module (source/modules/waf; a separate us-east-1 stack) ---
# Deploying the module builds a CLOUDFRONT-scope WebACL with default BLOCK and allow rules for the
# lists below (allow if IP OR country matches). Requires at least one of the two lists. Its deploy.sh
# prints the WebAclArn output to set as WAF_WEB_ACL_ARN in the root .env.
# Allowed viewer countries for the WAF geo rule, comma-separated ISO codes (e.g. US,CA,GB).
# WAF_ALLOWED_COUNTRIES=
# Allowed source IPv4 CIDRs for the WAF IP-set rule (e.g. 203.0.113.0/24,198.51.100.10/32).
# WAF_ALLOWED_IPS=
# With the SSAI module: allow manifests (*.m3u8/*.mpd) and the ad creatives MediaTailor fetches from AWS
# addresses; segments and keys stay behind the lists. See source/modules/waf/README.md.
# WAF_ALLOW_MANIFESTS=ON
# WAF_ALLOW_PATH_PREFIXES=/creatives/
